2 CONT =Laodice III=
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT '''Laodice III''' (in Greek Λαοδικη, died about 191 BC), was a Princess of Pontus and a daughter born to King Mithridates II of Pontus and his wife Laodice. Her sister was Laodice of Pontus and her brother was Mithridates III of P
2 CONC ontus. Laodice married her maternal first cousin, the Seleucid King Antiochus III the Great soon after his accession about 222 BC in a ceremony at Zeugma. She was proclaimed queen by Antiochus III at Antioch before he set out in h
2 CONC is expedition against Molon. The birth of their eldest child Antiochus, took place during the absence of the king on that expedition.[1] Laodice’s name does not appear in any sources; however her name is recorded in a number of in
2 CONC scriptions alongside with her husband’s in the later years of her husband’s reign at Sardis, Herakleia-by-Latmos (see Latmus), Iasos and Antioch. [2] When she died Antiochus III developed a cult for her and was granted divine hono
2 CONC rs alongside her husband at Teos. [3] Laodice III bore Antiochus III eight children who were: Antiochus, Seleucus IV Philopator, Ardys, an unnamed daughter who was engaged to Demetrius I of Bactria, Laodice IV, Cleopatra I Syra, A
2 CONC ntiochis and Antiochus IV Epiphanes born as Mithridates. After her death, Antiochus III married to Euboea of Chalcis, by whom he had no children. [4] [edit]
2 CONT
