2 CONT =Laodice II=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Laodice (Ancient Greek: Λαοδίκη Laodíkē; lived in the 3rd century BC), wife of her cousin Seleucus II Callinicus, was, according to the express statement of Polybius, the daughter of Andromachus and sister of Seleucid General Acha
2 CONC eus. Laodice II bore Seleucus II five children, among them were: Antiochis, Seleucus III Ceraunus and Antiochus III the Great.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laodice_II
