1 NOTE King of Pontus
2 CONT He committed suicide when his forces, with which he hoped to renew an attack
2 CONT on Rome, deserted him, and his son, Pharnaces II, rose up against him
2 CONT declaring himself King. Mithridates commanded his personal bodyguard to accept
2 CONT hisKin son as their king, and retired to a castle where he had himself killed.
2 CONT King of Pontus, as Mithradates VI , in northeastern Anatolia, Asia Minor
2 CONT 0121-0063 f Kr. King of the Bosphorus 0107-0063 B.C
1 NOTE Levde 132 - 069 f.Kr.
1 NOTE OR "MITHRENES""MITHRINES"; SATRAP OF ARMENIA FOR ALEXANDER THE GREAT
2 CONT 331BC-bef.317 BC; KING OF ARMENIA
1 NOTE "EUPATOR""DIONYSUS"; KNOWN AS "THE GREAT"; KING OF PONTUS 120-63 BC; ANNEXED THE
2 CONT KINGDOM OF THE BOSPORUS AND BECAME KING ca. 100 BC; ULTIMATELY DEFEATED IN THE
2 CONT THREE MITHRADATIC WARS (88-84, 83-81, 74-63) BY LUCIUS CORNELIUS SULLA, LUCIUS
2 CONT LUCINIUS MURENA, AND LICIUS LUCINIUS LUCULLUS WITH POMPEY THE GREAT
2 CONT RESPECTIVELY; FLEEING TO CRIMEA TO AVOID CAPTURE, HE ORDERED A SOLDIER TO KILL
2 CONT HIM; HAD MANY WIVES AND CONCUBINES
