1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cleopatra_III_of_Egypt
2 CONT
2 CONT Cleopatra III of Egypt
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Cleopatra III (Greek: Κλεοπάτρα, 161–101 BC) was queen of Egypt 142–101 BC.
2 CONT
2 CONT Cleopatra III was also known as Cleopatra Euergetis while associated with her husband Ptolemy VIII or her son Ptolemy X. She is attested as Cleopatra Philometor Soteira while associated with her eldest son Ptolemy IX. According to
2 CONC  Strabo she was sometimes known as Cleopatra Kokke when discussed in relation to her son Ptolemy X. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Joint rule with her mother and husband
2 CONT
2 CONT Ptolemy VIII first married Cleopatra III’s mother Cleopatra II in 145 BC, and married Cleopatra III in ca 139 BC. Cleopatra II rebelled against Ptolemy VIII in ca 132 BC. Cleopatra III fled to Cyprus in 130 BC with her husband Pto
2 CONC lemy VIII and was able to return to Alexandria in 127 BC. [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Cleopatra III and Ptolemy VIII had five children [1][4]:
2 CONT
2 CONT Ptolemy IX born ca 143 BC
2 CONT
2 CONT Tryphaena born ca 141 BC. Married Antiochus VIII Grypus, king of Syria in 124 BC
2 CONT
2 CONT Ptolemy X born ca 140 or 139 BC. Married his niece Berenice (daughter of Ptolemy IX and Cleopatra Selene I)
2 CONT
2 CONT Cleopatra IV born between 138 and 135 BC. Married first her brother Ptolemy IX and second Antiochus IX Cyzicenus, king of Syria
2 CONT
2 CONT Cleopatra Selene I born between 135 and 130 BC. Married first to her brother Ptolemy IX, and later to her brother Ptolemy X. Later married to Antiochus VIII Grypus, king of Syria, Antiochus IX Cyzicenus, king of Syria and Antiochu
2 CONC s X Eusebes, king of Syria.
2 CONT
2 CONT In ca 124 BC Cleopatra III and her husband were joined again by her mother Cleopatra II as a joint ruler.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joint Rule with her sons
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of Ptolemy VIII in 116 BC Cleopatra III ruled jointly with her mother Cleopatra II and her son Ptolemy IX. [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Cleopatra III expelled Ptolemy IX from Alexandria in 107 BC and replaced him as co-regent with her second son Ptolemy X. After 6 years of joint rule Ptolemy X had his mother Cleopatra III murdered in 101 BC. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cleopatra_III_of_Egypt
2 CONT
2 CONT Cleopatra III (Greek: Κλεοπάτρα, 161–101 BC) was queen of Egypt 142–101 BC.
2 CONT
