1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ziaelas_of_Bithynia
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT '''
2 CONT =Ziaelas of Bithynia=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Ziaelas (Greek: Ζιαήλας; lived c. 265 -228 BC, reigned c. 254-228 BC), third king of Bithynia, was a son of Nicomedes I and Ditizele.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Life'''
2 CONT
2 CONT After Nicomedes I died, his second wife Etazeta became ruler on behalf of her infant sons. The grown-up Ziaelas, excluded from the throne, had previously fled to Armenia and taken refuge at the court of King Arsames I in Sophene. 
2 CONC On his father's death he immediately endeavoured to regain his rights by force, he returned, aided by some Galatians. Although Etazeta was supported by neighbouring cities and Antigonus II Gonatas, Ziaelas rapidly conquered first 
2 CONC part, then all of Bithynia, forcing Etazeta and her sons to escape to Antigonus' court in Macedonia about 254 BC.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was succeeded by his son Prusias I about 228 BC after being killed by the Galatian Gauls. Like his father and his grandfather he also founded a new city named after him, Ziela, but the location of the city is unknown.[Note 3] H
2 CONC is daughter, born c. 245 BC, married Antiochus Hierax.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ziaelas_of_Bithynia
