1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''
2 CONT =Eurydice of Athens=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Eurydice (Greek: Εὐρυδίκη ἡ Ἀθηναία) was an Athenian woman of a family descended from the great Miltiades.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was first married to Macedonian Ophellas, the conqueror and king of Cyrene, and after his death returned to Athens, where she married Demetrius I of Macedon, on occasion of his first visit to that city. She is said to have had
2 CONC  by him a son called Corrhabus.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eurydice_of_Athens
