2 CONT =Cassander=
2 CONT  (brother of Antipater)
2 CONT
2 CONT Cassander (Greek: Κάσσανδρος) was a Greek Macedonian nobleman who lived in the 4th century BC.
2 CONT
2 CONT Cassander was the son of Iolaus by an unnamed mother and brother of the powerful Regent and general Antipater.[1] Cassander’s family were distant collateral relatives to the Argead dynasty.[2] Cassander, like Antipater, was origin
2 CONC ally from the Macedonian city of Paliura[3] and was a contemporary to Aristotle.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Little is known on his life. He married an unnamed Greek Macedonian noblewoman by whom he had a child: a daughter called Antigone[5] who married a Greek Macedonian nobleman called Magas[6] by whom she had a daughter called Berenic
2 CONC e I of Egypt.[7] His namesake was his nephew Cassander.
2 CONT
