2 CONT =Nysa=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Nysa or Nyssa (Greek: Νύσ(σ)α, flourished second half of 2nd century BC and first half of 1st century BC) was a Greek Princess from the Kingdom of Bithynia.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Biography'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Nysa was the daughter of the Monarchs Nicomedes III of Bithynia and Nysa. She was the namesake of her mother and had two brothers: Nicomedes IV of Bithynia who reigned as King from c. 94 BC to about 74 BC and Socrates Chrestus. Sh
2 CONC e was born and raised in Bithynia.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Suetonius (Caesar. 49), her cause was defended by the Roman Politician Gaius Julius Caesar in gratitude for her father's friendship.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nysa_(daughter_of_Nicomedes_III_of_Bithynia)
