2 CONT Shatadhanvan (IAST: Śatadhanvan) or Shatadhanus was a king of the Maurya dynasty. He ruled from 195–187 BC. According to the Puranas, he was the successor of Devavarman Maurya and reigned for eight years. During his time, the empi
2 CONC re lost some of its territories because of invasions. He was succeeded by Brihadratha Maurya.
2 CONT
