2 CONT
2 CONT Apame IV, sometimes known as Apama IV (Greek: Απάμα Δ΄) was a princess from the Antigonid dynasty. Her father was Philip V, King from 221 BC to 179 BC and her brother was Perseus, King from 179 BC to 167 BC. She was the wife of Ki
2 CONC ng Prusias II Cynegus of Bithynia, and mother of his successor, Nicomedes II Epiphanes. Her husband was her cousin because her aunt Apama III, was the wife of Prusias I Cholus.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
