2 CONT Phthia (in Greek Φθία; lived 4th century BC), was a Greek queen, daughter of Menon of Pharsalus, the Thessalian hipparch, and wife of Aeacides, king of Epirus, by whom she became the mother of the celebrated Pyrrhus, as well as of
2 CONC  two daughters: Deidamia, the wife of Demetrius Poliorcetes, and Troias, of whom nothing more is known.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her portrait is found on some of the coins of her son Pyrrhus.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
