2 CONT =Polycratia of Argos=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Polycratia (Greek: Πολυκρατία) (fl. 213 BC) was an Argive woman who had married Aratus the Younger, the son of the great Achaean statesman Aratus of Sicyon. She probably gave him a son, also named Aratus, who later became an ambas
2 CONC sador of the Achaean League. When Aratus and his son came to the court of Macedon, Polycratia was seduced by the young king Philip V who later resolved to have her father-in-law and her husband poisoned. Some sources state that sh
2 CONC e actually married Philip and became the mother of his son Perseus, who succeeded his father in 179 BC.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polycratia_of_Argos
