1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''
2 CONT =Bas of Bithynia=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Bas (Greek: Bάς; lived c. 397 BC – 326 BC, ruled 376 BC – 326 BC), first independent ruler of Bithynia, governed fifty years, from 376 to 326 BC, and died at the age of 71.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Life'''
2 CONT
2 CONT He succeeded his father Boteiras, and was himself succeeded by his own son Zipoetes I.
2 CONT
2 CONT He defeated Calas, a general of Alexander the Great, and maintained the independence of Bithynia.
2 CONT
