1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''
2 CONT =Asinnalus of Media Atropatene=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Asinnalus of Media Atropatene (flourished 1st century BC) was a Prince who served as a King of Media Atropatene.
2 CONT
2 CONT Little is known on the origins and life of Asinnalus. He was a monarch of Median and possibly of Armenian, Greek descent. He succeeded his relative Artavasdes I in the Kingship of Media Atropatene in 30 BC. As in that year the Rom
2 CONC an Triumvir Octavian, gave Artavasdes I the Kingdom of Sophene to govern as a Roman Client King.
2 CONT
2 CONT Asinnalus ruled as King of Media Atropatene from 30 BC to an unknown date in the 20s BC. He is only known from surviving numismatic evidence. He appeared to have died at an unknown date in the 20s BC, as he was succeeded by Arioba
2 CONC rzanes II, one of the sons of Artavasdes I.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asinnalus_of_Media_Atropatene
