1 NOTE {geni:about_me} source:  http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alcetas_I
2 CONT
2 CONT Alcetas I (Greek: Ἀλκέτας), (390, 385 - 370 BC) king of Epirus, was the son of Tharypus. For a reason, of which we are not informed, he was expelled from his kingdom, and took refuge with Dionysius I of Syracuse, by whom he was re
2 CONC instated. After his restoration we find him the ally of the Athenians, and of Jason of Pherae, the Tagus of Thessaly. In 373 BC, he appeared at Athens with Jason, for the purpose of defending Athenian general Timotheus, who, throu
2 CONC gh their influence, was acquitted. On his death the kingdom, which till then had been governed by one king, was divided between his two sons, Neoptolemus I and Arybbas.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] ReferencesPausanias (i. 11. § 3). Demosthenes against Timotheus (pp. 1187, 1190). Diodorus (xv. 13. 36.). [edit] SourcesThis article incorporates text from the public domain Dictionary of Greek and Roman Biography and Mytho
2 CONC logy by William Smith (1870). Preceded by Tharrhypas King of Epirus 390– 370 BC Succeeded by Neoptolemus I and Arybbas  Persondata  Name Alcetas 01 Of Epirus  Alternative names   Short description   Date of birth   Place of birth 
2 CONC   Date of death   Place of death  
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT '''
2 CONT =Alcetas I of Epirus=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Alcetas I (Greek: Ἀλκέτας) (390/385-370 BC) was a king of Epirus, the son of Tharrhypas.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Biography'''
2 CONT
2 CONT He was expelled from his kingdom for unknown reasons, and took refuge with Dionysius I of Syracuse, by whom he was reinstated.
2 CONT
2 CONT After his restoration, he allied with the Athenians, and with Jason of Pherae, the Tagus of Thessaly. In 373 BC, he appeared at Athens with Jason, for the purpose of defending Athenian general Timotheus, who, through their influen
2 CONC ce, was acquitted.
2 CONT
2 CONT Upon his death, the kingdom was divided between his two sons, Neoptolemus I and Arybbas.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alcetas_I_of_Epirus
