1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''
2 CONT =Phraates V=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Phraates V (Persian: فرهاد پنجم‎‎), known by the diminutive Phraataces (Ancient Greek: Φραατάκης), ruled the Parthian Empire from 2 BC to AD 4. He was the younger son of Phraates IV of Parthia (37-2 BC) and Musa of Parthia, with w
2 CONC hom he is associated on his coins. Under Phraates V a war threatened to break out with Rome about the supremacy in Armenia and Media. But when Augustus (27 BC-AD 14) sent his adopted son Gaius Caesar into the east in order to inva
2 CONC de Iran, the Parthians preferred to conclude a treaty (AD 1), by which once again Armenia was recognized as in the Roman sphere. Soon afterwards Phraates V and his mother were slain by the Parthians, about 4. Josephus alleges that
2 CONC  Phraates V married his mother Musa, and, this being unacceptable to the Parthians, they rose up and overthrew him, offering the crown to Orodes III of Parthia (who ruled briefly in 6).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phraates_V
