1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Alexander of Megalopolis==
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_of_Megalopolis En]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Alexander''' of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Megalopolis,_Greece Megalopolis] (Greek: Ἀλέξανδρος) was originally a Macedonian, but he received the franchise and was settled at Arcadian Megalopolis about 190 BC. He '''pretende
2 CONC d to be a descendant''' of [https://www.geni.com/people/Alexander-the-Great-king-of-Macedonia/6000000007875679261 '''Alexander the Great'''], and accordingly, he called his two sons [https://www.geni.com/people/Philip-of-Megalopol
2 CONC is/6000000205411213828 '''Philip'''] and [https://www.geni.com/people/Alexander-of-Megalopolis/6000000205410898883 '''Alexander''']. His daughter [https://www.geni.com/people/Apama/6000000205410898836 '''Apama'''] was married to [
2 CONC https://www.geni.com/people/Amynander-of-Athamania/6000000205410617831 '''Amynander'''] king of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Athamanians Athamanians]. Her eldest brother [https://www.geni.com/people/Philip-of-Megalopolis/6000000
2 CONC 205411213828 '''Philip'''], followed her to her court, and being of vain character, he allowed himself to be tempted with the prospect of gaining possession to the throne of Macedonia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note:''' 
2 CONT * '''He was not biological son and descendant of''' [https://www.geni.com/people/Alexander-the-Great-king-of-Macedonia/6000000007875679261 '''Alexander the Great'''], '''he was  just''' '''pretended to be a his descendant.''' '''T
2 CONC here is no existed any proofs and physically vital realistic written historical evidences who states and confirmed that he was''' [https://www.geni.com/people/Alexander-the-Great-king-of-Macedonia/6000000007875679261 '''Alexander'
2 CONC s'''] '''descendant.'''
