1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Grabos I===
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grabos_I En]
2 CONT
2 CONT Grabos (or Grabus; Greek: Γράβος) was an [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Illyrians Illyrian] chieftain who is mentioned once in an Athenian inscription in 423 BC. He or his son (possibly [https://www.geni.com/people/Sirrhas/6000000
2 CONC 006101322857 '''Sirras''']) were the leaders of the Illyrians who supported the Lyncestians against an expedition by the Macedonians in 423 BC.[1] The Illyrian-Lyncestian troops defeated the Macedonian-Spartan alliance.
2 CONT
2 CONT He probably was the grandfather of [https://www.geni.com/people/Grabos-II-Illyrian-King-of-Taulantia-c-358-356-BC/6000000205380959848 '''Grabos II'''].
2 CONT
2 CONT ====[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grabos_I#See_also See also]====
2 CONT
