1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Grabos II===
2 CONT
2 CONT Grabus[1] (also Grabos;[2] Greek: Γράβος; ruled c. 358 – 356 BC) was an Illyrian king who reigned in southern Illyria in the 4th century BC. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grabos_II En], [https://hr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grabos Hr], [https://bs.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grabos Bs],  [https://hu.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grabosz_ill%C3%ADr_kir%C3%A1ly Hu], [https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki
2 CONC /Grabo It]
2 CONT
2 CONT ====[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grabos_II#Biography Biography]====
2 CONT
2 CONT According to a historical reconstruction, Grabus belonged to the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grabaei Grabaei], an Illyrian tribe mentioned by [https://www.geni.com/people/Pliny-the-Elder/6000000011395982289 '''Pliny the Elder''
2 CONC '] (23–79 AD), although the tribe may have been incorporated into the Taulantii realm of which Grabus became king.[1] It has been further conjectured that after [https://www.geni.com/people/Phillip-II-The-One-Eye-king-of-Macedonia
2 CONC /6000000008248160118 '''Philip II of Macedon'''] defeated [https://www.geni.com/people/Bardylis-I-king-of-Dardania/6000000011730996286 '''Bardylis'''] (c. 358 BC), the Grabaei, under Grabus, became the most powerful tribe in Illyr
2 CONC ia.[3][2]
2 CONT
2 CONT In 356 BC, Athens formed an alliance with Grabus, [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paeonia_(kingdom)_ Paeonian] king [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lyppeius Lyppeius], and [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thracians Thracian] king [htt
2 CONC ps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cetriporis Cetriporis] against [https://www.geni.com/people/Phillip-II-The-One-Eye-king-of-Macedonia/6000000008248160118 '''Philip''']. Some months later the three northern kings were defeated by Philip'
2 CONC s general [https://www.geni.com/people/Parmenion/6000000011772808565 '''Parmenion'''], while the Athenians were otherwise engaged in the Aegean Sea.[4] 
2 CONT
2 CONT ====[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grabos_II#See_also See also]====
2 CONT
2 CONT ====[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grabos_II#References References]====
2 CONT
2 CONT ====[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grabos_II#Bibliography Bibliography]====
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://enciklopedija.cc/wiki/Grabos Grabos]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note:''' See profile of [https://www.geni.com/people/Grabos-I-king-of-Taulantia-437-423-BC/6000000205380658823 '''Grabos I.''']
