1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Pythodorida of Pontus===
2 CONT Titles:
2 CONT *Queen of Pontus
2 CONT *Queen consort of the Bosporan Kingdom
2 CONT *Queen consort of Cilicia
2 CONT *Queen consort of Cappadocia
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouses:
2 CONT *King Polemon I of Pontus
2 CONT *King Archelaus of Cappadocia
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue:
2 CONT *Artaxias III of Armenia
2 CONT *Polemon II of Pontus
2 CONT *Antonia Tryphaena, Queen of Thrace
2 CONT
2 CONT Father:
2 CONT *Pythodoros of Tralles
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother:
2 CONT *Antonia
2 CONT
2 CONT Born:
2 CONT *30 BC or 29 BC Smyrna
2 CONT
2 CONT Died:
2 CONT *AD 38 (aged 67 or 68) Pontus
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Pythodorida or Pythodoris of Pontus (Greek: Πυθοδωρίδα or Πυθοδωρίς, 30 BC or 29 BC – 38) was a Roman Client Queen of Pontus, the Bosporan Kingdom, Cilicia and Cappadocia.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins & Early Life===
2 CONT
2 CONT Pythodorida is also known as Pythodoris I and Pantos Pythodorida. According to an honorific inscription dedicated to her in Athens Greece in the late 1st century BC, her royal title was Queen Pythodorida Philometor (Greek: ΒΑΣΙΛΙΣ
2 CONC ΣΑ ΠΥΘΟΔΩΡΙΔΑ ΦΙΛΟΜΗΤΩΡ). Philometor means "mother-loving" and this title is associated with the Greek Pharaohs and Queens of the Ptolemaic dynasty of Ancient Egypt.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pythodorida was born and raised in Smyrna (modern İzmir, Turkey). She was the daughter and only child of wealthy Anatolian Greek and friend to the late triumvir Pompey, Pythodoros of Tralles and Antonia. Pythodorida was half Roman
2 CONC  and half Anatolian Greek. She was the namesake of her father.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her maternal grandparents were the Roman triumvir Mark Antony and Antonia Hybrida Minor, who were paternal first cousins, however Pythodorida’s paternal grandparents are unknown. Pythodorida seems to the first-born grandchild born
2 CONC  to the triumvir Antony.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Queen===
2 CONT
2 CONT About 14 BC, Pythodorida married King Polemon Pythodoros of Pontus as his second wife. She became Queen of Pontus and the Bosporan Kingdom when she married Polemon I. Polemon I was previously widowed by his first wife and had no n
2 CONC atural children, except for a stepson.
2 CONT Pythodorida and Polemon had two sons and one daughter, who were:
2 CONT *Zenon, also known as Zeno-Artaxias or Artaxias III, who became King of Armenia in 18 and reigned until his death in 35
2 CONT *Marcus Antonius Polemon Pythodoros, also known as Polemon II of Pontus
2 CONT *Antonia Tryphaena who married King of Thrace, Cotys VIII
2 CONT
2 CONT Polemon I died in 8 BC and Pythodorida became the sole Queen of Pontus until her death. Pythodorida was able to retain Colchis and Cilicia but the Bosporan Kingdom, she was unable to retain. The Bosporan Kingdom, was succeeded by 
2 CONC her first husband's stepson Aspurgus.
2 CONT
2 CONT After Polemon I died, she married King Archelaus of Cappadocia. Archelaus and Pythodorida had no children. Through her marriages, she became Roman Client Queen of Cappadocia. Pythodorida had moved with her children from Pontus to 
2 CONC Cappadocia to live with Archelaus. When Archelaus died in 17, Cappadocia became a Roman province and she returned with her family back to Pontus. In later years, Polemon II assisted his mother in the administration of the kingdom.
2 CONC  When Pythodorida died, Polemon II succeeded her. Pythodorida was a friend and contemporary to the Greek geographer Strabo. Strabo is said to have described Pythodorida as a woman of virtuous character. Strabo considered her to ha
2 CONC ve a great capacity for business and considered that under Pythodorida’s rule, Pontus had flourished.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sources===
2 CONT
2 CONT *Vassal - Queens and Some Contemporary Women of the Roman Empire by Grace Harriet Macurdy (1937)
2 CONT *http://www.ancientlibrary.com/smith-bio/2962.html
2 CONT *http://www.guide2womenleaders.com/turkey_substates.htm
2 CONT *http://www.tyndalehouse.com/egypt/ptolemies/cleopatra_vii_fr.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pythodorida_of_Pontus
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>__________
2 CONT http://www.american-pictures.com/genealogy/persons/per01339.htm#0
2 CONT
2 CONT ===[http://www.geni.com/discussions/109760?msg=795293   Not the mother of Archelaus]===
2 CONT Despite the reference above from: http://www.american-pictures.com/genealogy/persons/per01339.htm#0, that places her as the mother of  Archelaus Minor,  no other reference cites Pythodorida as his or his sister, Glaphyra’s, mother
2 CONC . Eg: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pythodorida_of_Pontus
2 CONT
2 CONT In the http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Archelaus_of_Cappadocia article about Archelaus & Glaphyra’s father, Pythdorida is explicitly stated to have been his second wife, with whom he had no children.  Here http://en.wikipedia.org/wik
2 CONC i/Glaphyra it states “Glaphyra's mother, the first wife of Archelaus, was an Armenian Princess whose name is unknown and who died by 8 BCE”
2 CONT
2 CONT I am therefore removing Pythodorida as the mother of Archelaus. [Sharon June 2012]
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT '''
2 CONT =Pythodorida of Pontus=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Pythodorida or Pythodoris of Pontus (Greek: Πυθοδωρίδα or Πυθοδωρίς, 30 BC or 29 BC – 38) was a Roman Client Queen of Pontus, the Bosporan Kingdom, Cilicia and Cappadocia.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Origins & Early Life'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Pythodorida is also known as Pythodoris I and Pantos Pythodorida. According to an honorific inscription dedicated to her in Athens Greece in the late 1st century BC, her royal title was Queen Pythodorida Philometor (Greek: ΒΑΣΙΛΙΣ
2 CONC ΣΑ ΠΥΘΟΔΩΡΙΔΑ ΦΙΛΟΜΗΤΩΡ). Philometor means "mother-loving" and this title is associated with the Greek Pharaohs and Queens of the Ptolemaic dynasty of Ancient Egypt.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pythodorida was born and raised in Smyrna (modern İzmir, Turkey). She was the daughter and only child of wealthy Anatolian Greek and friend to the late triumvir Pompey, Pythodoros of Tralles and Antonia. Pythodorida was half Roman
2 CONC  and half Anatolian Greek. She was the namesake of her father.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her maternal grandparents were the Roman triumvir Mark Antony and Antonia Hybrida Minor, who were paternal first cousins, however Pythodorida’s paternal grandparents are unknown. Pythodorida seems to the first-born grandchild born
2 CONC  to the triumvir Antony.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Queen'''
2 CONT
2 CONT About 14 BC, Pythodorida married King Polemon Pythodoros of Pontus as his second wife. She became Queen of Pontus and the Bosporan Kingdom when she married Polemon I. Polemon I was previously widowed by his first wife and had no n
2 CONC atural children, except for a stepson.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pythodorida and Polemon had two sons and one daughter, who were:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Zenon, also known as Zeno-Artaxias or Artaxias III, who became King of Armenia in 18 and reigned until his death in 35
2 CONT * Marcus Antonius Polemon Pythodoros, also known as Polemon II of Pontus
2 CONT * Antonia Tryphaena who married King of Thrace, Cotys VIII
2 CONT
2 CONT Polemon I died in 8 BC and Pythodorida became the sole Queen of Pontus until her death. Pythodorida was able to retain Colchis and Cilicia but the Bosporan Kingdom, she was unable to retain. The Bosporan Kingdom, was succeeded by 
2 CONC her first husband's stepson Aspurgus.
2 CONT
2 CONT After Polemon I died, she married King Archelaus of Cappadocia. Archelaus and Pythodorida had no children. Through her marriages, she became Roman Client Queen of Cappadocia. Pythodorida had moved with her children from Pontus to 
2 CONC Cappadocia to live with Archelaus. When Archelaus died in 17, Cappadocia became a Roman province and she returned with her family back to Pontus.
2 CONT
2 CONT In later years, Polemon II assisted his mother in the administration of the kingdom. When Pythodorida died, Polemon II succeeded her. Pythodorida was a friend and contemporary to the Greek geographer Strabo. Strabo is said to have
2 CONC  described Pythodorida as a woman of virtuous character. Strabo considered her to have a great capacity for business and considered that under Pythodorida’s rule, Pontus had flourished.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pythodorida_of_Pontus
