2 CONC in 626 BC to his death in 605 BC. Though initially only aimed at restoring and securing the independence of Babylonia, Nabopolassar's uprising against the Neo-Assyrian Empire, which had ruled Babylonia for more than a century, eve
2 CONC ntually led to the complete destruction of the Assyrian Empire and the rise of the Neo-Babylonian Empire in its place. .. ... ....
