1 NOTE {geni:about_me} = Aspacures III (or Varaz-Bakur II, Georgian=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Mihrdat III, king of Iberia 
2 CONT * Aspacures III (or Varaz-Bakur II , Georgian : ვარაზ-ბაკურ II ), of the Chosroid Dynasty , was the king of Iberia ( Kartli , eastern Georgia ) from c. 380 to 394. He was the son and successor of Mirdat III and was married to the 
2 CONC daughter of Trdat , his relative and successor. He is credited by the Georgian chronicles with the construction of the Tsilkani church . [1] During his reign, the Roman Empire signed the Peace of Acylisene with Sassanid Iranin whi
2 CONC ch he admitted the loss of Iberia and a larger share of Armenia . His sons were Pharasmanes and Mihrdat .
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://www.conflicts.rem33.com/images/Georgia/KArtlis%20Tskhovreba.htm CONCISE HISTORY OF THE OF THE GEORGIANS]
2 CONT
