1 NOTE {geni:about_me} >'''en.Wikipedia, [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iamblichus_of_Apameia Iamblichus of Apameia]''' (6 Jan 2015):
2 CONT >"Iamblichus was an Ancient Greek Neoplatonic philosopher of Apameia (Syria), and a contemporary of the emperor Julian the Apostate (331–363) and Libanius. He was thought to have committed suicide during the last year of Valens' r
2 CONC eign (378 CE).[1]\
2 CONT >"He is often confused with Iamblichus Chalcidensis but the time at which he lived, and his intimacy with Julian, show that he belongs to a later date. The emperor, where he speaks of him, bestows extravagant praise upon him.[2] 
