1 NOTE {geni:about_me} --------------------
2 CONT '''
2 CONT =Anicius Petronius Probus=
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT Flavius Anicius Petronius Probus (floruit 395-406) was a politician of the Western Roman Empire.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Biography'''
2 CONT
2 CONT A member of the gens Anicia, he was the son of Sextus Claudius Petronius Probus (consul in 371) and of Anicia Faltonia Proba; his elder brothers were Anicius Hermogenianus Olybrius and Anicius Probinus (consuls in 395), his sister
2 CONC  Anicia Proba.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 395, he is attested as quaestor elected (by the Emperor), in 406 was consul with the Eastern Emperor Arcadius as colleague; one of his consular diptychs is preserved at the Museo del tesoro della cattedrale di Aosta, and depict
2 CONC s Emperor Honorius.
2 CONT
2 CONT Probus was a Christian.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source : '''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anicius_Petronius_Probus
