1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Rufius Viventius Gallus From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Rufius Viventius Gallus (mid 5th-century) was a Roman politician, who was urban prefect in the mid 5th-century.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Flavius Avitus Marinianus and wife Anastasia.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married his cousin Aviena
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT * [https://books.google.com/books?id=G5W6vCO_pYUC&lpg=PA492&ots=8kYydbhwqA&dq=Rufius%20Viventius%20Gallus&pg=PA492#v=onepage&q=Rufius%20Viventius%20Gallus&f=false page 492] of The Prosopography of the Later Roman Empire: A.D. 395-
2 CONC 527, Parts 395-527 By Arnold Hugh Martin Jones, John Robert Martindale, J. Morris
