2 CONT The meaning of the word, parricide.
2 CONT The word has its origins in old Latin.
2 CONT Parricidam Parricidum.
2 CONT Parri means kin or relative.
2 CONT A parricide is one who murders one's father, mother, or other near relatives.
2 CONT The word Patricide is also coming from this root word.
