1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Eparchius Philagrius
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT  Jump to: navigation, search
2 CONT
2 CONT Flavius Eparchius Philagrius (c. 338 - aft. 382) was a Roman politician and religious figure.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Flavius Philagrius and wife. He served as a notarius between 361 and 363 and rose to comes Orientis in 382
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Egnatia Avita Severa, born c. 355, daughter of Quintus Flavius Egnatius Placidus Severus and wife Antonia Marcianilla, and had three sons: Eparchius, born c. 360, vir nobilis in Tullum Leucorum, Gallia, who married and 
2 CONC was the father of Lupus of Troyes and Vincentius, a Priest and bishop of Mediolanum Santonum, Gallia Aquitania; Flavius Julius Agricola; and Lysticius, born c. 375.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT References
2 CONT  Christian Settipani. Continuité gentilice et continuité sénatoriale dans les familles sénatoriales romaines à l'époque impériale, 2000
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.Jump up ^ http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=bernd-jansen&id=I47188
