1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lupo_del_Friuli<br/>
2 CONT -https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lupus_of_Friuli
2 CONT
2 CONT == MedLands ==
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. '''LUPUS''' (-killed in battle --).  Duke of Friulia.  Paulus Diaconus records that "Lupus" succeeded as Duke of Friulia on the death of Ago, and was attacked by the khagan of the Avars and killed[194], but neither event can be
2 CONC  dated from the primary sources so far consulted.  <br/>
2 CONT '''m''' ---.  The name and origin of Duke Lupus's wife are not known.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Duke Lupus & his wife had two children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT > a) AMEFRIT (-Nemas --).  Paulus Diaconus names "Amefrit, eius filius [Lupo]" when recording that he claimed the succession after his father was killed but was expelled by the army of King Grimoald, fled to the Slavs and died "ap
2 CONC ut Nemas castrum"[195]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT > b) THEUDERADA (-after 690).  Paulus Diaconus records that "Grimualdus rex…suo filio Romualdo" married "Lupo duce…filiam eius Theuderadam" after her father's death[196].  "Theuderada" is named wife of Duke Romuald in the Benedict
2 CONC i Chronicon, but her origin is not given[197].  Romuald married her after her father, who had rebelled against King Grimoald, was killed.  She was regent in 690 during the minority of her son Duke Gisulf[198].  '''m''' ([664]) ROM
2 CONC UALD, son of GRIMOALD I Duke of Benevento, King of the Lombards & his first wife --- (-687).  He succeeded his father in 671 as ROMUALD I Duke of Benevento. 
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORTHERN%20ITALY%20900-1100.htm#ArichisIBeneventoA, visited Dec. 2020.
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT * ''Merged with Lupi Family Board  (recent studies, therefore secondary sources) '' https://www.geni.com/discussions/220714?msg=1425791 <br/>
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.genmarenostrum.com/pagine-lettere/letteral/Lupis/Stirpe_Luporum.html#CAPOSTIPITE_DEI_LUPI_DI_SORAGNA_1198
2 CONT
2 CONT *6.3. Lupo (* 525 or 550 + after 603 AD) To be identified in all probability with that Lupo who was Duke of Champagne 575-81. He lived at the court of King Sigebert of which he was Councilor v. G. Zonta, G. Balsamo-Crivelli, "Hist
2 CONC ory of Italian literature", Volume 1, Turin 1932, p. 38: "Venantius brought among the grim brutality of the Merovingians a flash of refinement, culture and Roman civilization, so much more suited to him the pride that he attribute
2 CONC s to Lupo , adviser to Sigebert:" Under you, Rome she returned here and lives again ".  Married Catelinda del Friuli, grand daughter of Agone, duke of Friuli from 653 to 662.  Their children:
2 CONT **7.6. Lupo or Lupone duke of Friuli He was made duke in 662; died in battle in 647 AD (+ Friuli 663) Paolo Diacono narrates: "When Agone died, Lupo was made duke (662). These, for a road that in ancient times had been built acros
2 CONC s the sea (it must have been an" overpass "that united Aquileia a Grado Ndr.), Entered the island of Grado with the cavalry; he sacked the city and recovered and took away the treasures that had been transferred from Aquileia.  Ma
2 CONC rried Amilda or Ermelinda "Schiavona" (ie of the Slavs, of Dalmatia) marquise of some castles in Friuli. cfr .: G. Santini, "Medieval Europe: introduction to the study of territorial structures of public law: lessons in the histor
2 CONC y of Italian law", 1986, pag. 174
2 CONT ***8.1. Sisulfo (Gisulfo) &  Romilda, daughter of Giulio. Calandrini in "Il Publio svezzese", cit., Disputes the assertion of Paolo Diacono according to which Romilda was the wife of the Duke of Friuli Gisulfo.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lupus_of_Friuli
2 CONT
2 CONT >Lupus' son Arnefrit claimed Friuli on his father's death, but was unseated by Grimoald. Lupus' daughter Theuderada (or Theodorada) married the aforementioned Romuald. She acted as regent of Benevento for their son Gisulf.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT  7.6. Lupo o Lupone duca del Friuli 
2 CONT
2 CONT Fu fatto duca nel 662; morto in battaglia nel 647 AD (+ Friuli 663)  Narra Paolo Diacono: "Morto Agone, fu fatto duca Lupo (662). Questi, per una strada che in antico era stata costruita attraverso il mare (doveva essere una "sopr
2 CONC aelevata" che univa Aquileia a Grado Ndr.), entrò con la cavalleria nell'isola di Grado; mise a sacco la città e recuperò e portò via i tesori che erano stati trasferiti da Aquileia
2 CONT
2 CONT  = Amilda o Ermelinda "Schiavona"(cioè degli Slavi, della Dalmazia) marchesa di alcuni castelli in Friuli. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ''cfr.: G. Santini, "Europa medioevale: introduzione allo studio delle strutture territoriali di diritto pubblico : lezioni di storia del diritto italiano", 1986,`pag. 174''
