1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Gallus Magnus''' (?-after 562), was a Gallo-Roman Senator, a Patrician of Narbonne, and Bishop of Troyes (562). His grave is known and has an inscription identifying him.
2 CONT ****** Wikipedia - Roman Catholic Diocese of Troyes Listed as Bishop of Troyes:
2 CONT
2 CONT Gallomagnus, 573–582[41] Gallomagnus participated in the Council of Paris of 573: L. Sirmond, Conciliorum Galliae Collectio I (Paris: Didot 1789), p. 1197; and in the First Council of Mâcon: Sirmond, p. 1244.
2 CONT
