1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -http://www.genmarenostrum.com/pagine-lettere/letteral/Lupis/Stirpe_Luporum.html
2 CONT
2 CONT 8.1. Sisulfo (Gisulfo)
2 CONT
2 CONT  = Romilda, figlia di Giulio. Il Calandrini ne “Il Publio svezzese”, cit., contesta l’asserzione di Paolo Diacono secondo la quale Romilda sarebbe stata la moglie del Duca del Friuli Gisulfo
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------
2 CONT ------------
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Profiles inserted on the basis of studies on secondary sources of the Lupi Family table,'' <br/>
2 CONT ''but interesting correspondence on bulk primary source MedLands 2020 profiles: ''<br/>
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORTHERN%20ITALY%20900-1100.htm#GisulfFriulia
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         GISULF (-killed in battle Friulia 610).  The primary source which confirms that Gisulf was the son of Duke Gisulf I has not yet been identified.  He succeeded his father as GISULF II Duke of Friulia.  Paulus Diaconus re
2 CONC cords that "Gaidoaldus dux de Tridento et Gisulfus de Foroiuli" rebelled against Agilolf King of the Lombards but were pardoned[172].  His importance as ruler in Friulia is shown by Paulus Diaconus specifying that the installation
2 CONC  of "Iohannes" as Patriarch of Aquileja was "cum consensu regis et Gisulfi ducis"[173].  Paulus Diaconus records that "rex Avarum" launched another invasion during which "Gisulfus Foroiulianis dux" was killed[174].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ROMILDA, daughter of ---.  Paulus Diaconus names "Romilda" as wife of "Gisulfus Foroiulanus dux", when he records her escape with her children after her husband was killed[175].  
2 CONT
2 CONT   Duke Gisulf & his wife had eight children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT *d)         GRIMOALD (-671, bur Ticinum, Basilica of St Ambrosius).  Paulus Diaconus names "Taso et Cacco iam adulescentes, Raduald…et Grimuald adhuc in puerili ætate" as the sons of "Gisulfus Foroiulanus dux", when recording Grim
2 CONC oald's difficulty in escaping after the death of their father[182].  Paulus Diaconus records that "Radoald…et Grimoald" went to Benevento to join "Arichis Beneventanorum ducem"[183].  He fled to Benevento with his brother Radoald 
2 CONC after the execution of their two older brothers.  He succeeded his brother in [647/48] as GRIMOALD I Duke of Benevento. -        DUKES of BENEVENTO. 
