2 CONT # https://www.werelate.org/wiki/Person:Maurilion_De_Angouleme_%281%29
2 CONT # https://www.werelate.org/wiki/Person:Ingund_Unknown_%281%29 Married Ingonde, Ingund, or Ingunda (born c. 499, Thuringia d. 546) was a queen of the Franks by marriage to Clotaire I. She was the daughter of King Baderic of Thuring
2 CONC ia (c. 480 - c. 529). She was the mother of Charibert I, Guntram, and Sigebert I. She was the sister of one of Clotaire's other wives, Aregund.
2 CONT # http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ingund does not show a 2nd marriage for Ingund 
2 CONT # WikiTree contributors, "Maurilion (d'Angouleme) Angoulême (0520-abt.0562)," WikiTree: The Free Family Tree, (https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/D'Angouleme-13 : accessed 06 June 2025).  Son of Florentius (de Genève) de Geneve and Art
2 CONC hémie (de Lyons).  comments: “Need citation for Palatine as his daughter. Wikipedia's citations lack or don't exist. Palatine, is also cited as the daughter of Gallomagnus of Troyes.[1]”
2 CONT #-https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Munderic According to Christian Settipani, Munderic married Arthemia, the granddaughter of Rusticus, archbishop of Lyon, and they were the parents of the wife of the Frankish nobleman, Mummolin,[2] 
2 CONC although others have referred to him as Munderic's son.
2 CONT # https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Troyes-2 Daughter of Gallomagnus Troyes and [mother unknown]
