1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT Vichitravirya (Sanskrit: विचित्रवीर्य, vicitravīrya) was a king in Indian Religious Texts. In the Mahabharata he was the younger son of queen Satyavati and king Shantanu and grandfather of the Pandavas and Kauravas.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT BEFORE HE ATTAINED TO MAJARITY, CHITRANGADA, HAD BEEN SLAIN BY THE GANDHARVAS.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT As the name suggests(vichitra = strangeness), so not sure if he was weak or eunuch or homosexual.  So, general perception was that he can't get a wife.
