0 @N6000000002188198468@ NOTE Vasumitra
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Vasumitra or Sumitra (as per one manuscript of Matsya Purana) (131 - 124 BCE) was the fourth Sunga ruler. He was the son of Agnimitra by his queen Dharini.
1 CONT
1 CONT Kalidasa's Malavikagnimitram tells us that he guarded the sacrificial horse let looes by his grandfather Pushyamitra and he defeated a 'Yavana' (Indo-Greek) army on the banks of of river Sindhu (Indus)(Act V, 14). Bana's Harshacha
1 CONC rita mentioned him as Sumitra and informs us that he was killed by Mitradeva (or Muladeva) while enjoying a drama.
1 CONT Preceded by
1 CONT Vasujyeshtha Sunga ruler
1 CONT circa 131 BCE Succeeded by
1 CONT Andhraka
1 CONT
