0 @N6000000002187622969@ NOTE Berenice IV of Egypt
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Berenice IV (Greek: ?e?e????), was the daughter of Ptolemy XII of Egypt and probably Cleopatra V of Egypt Tryphaena, sister of Cleopatra VI of Egypt Tryphaena, and the famous Cleopatra VII (loved by Julius Caesar and Mark Antony).
1 CONC  Berenice dethroned her father in 58 BC and became co-regent with her mother. They ruled Egypt for a year, until her mother died and she ruled alone.
1 CONT
1 CONT As a lone woman ruling Egypt, she was expected to marry and have a man as a co-regent. When she did not, her consuls forced her to marry Seleucus Kybiosaktes, but she had him strangled and remained as sole ruler. She later married
1 CONC  Archelaus, but he was not co-regent. However, her reign ended in 55 BC when her father took the throne and had her executed.
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Ptolemy XII Ptolemaic Queen of Egypt
1 CONT with Cleopatra V Succeeded by:
1 CONT Ptolemy XII
