0 @N6000000002187617043@ NOTE Ashur-dan II
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT
1 CONT Ashur-Dan II was King of Assyria. He succeeded his father, Tiglath-Pileser II, in 935 and reigned until his death in 912 BC, when he was succeeded by his son Adad-nirari II.
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Tiglath-Pileser II King of Assyria
1 CONT 934–912 BC Succeeded by:
1 CONT Adad-nirari II 
