0 @N6000000002187617082@ NOTE Ashur-resh-ishi II
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT
1 CONT Ashur-resh-ishi II was King of Assyria for five years. He succeeded his long-reigning father Ashur-rabi II in 972 and reigned until his death in 967 BC, when he was succeeded by his son, Tiglath-Pileser II. Little is known about h
1 CONC is reign, which was a time of political eclipse for Assyria.
