1 CONT faith. At his death, his kingdom was divided between his four sons, Gundobad,
1 CONT Godegesil, Chilperic, and Gundomar. Later, Gundobad murdered brother
1 CONT Chilperic and his consort/wife, forcing their two daughters to take refuge in
1 CONT Geneva with uncle Godegesil. Clovis, hearing good reports of the one
1 CONT daughter, Clotilda, obtained permission for marriage from Gundobad, a
1 CONT marriage yielding 4 sons, 3 to become future kings.
0 @N6000000002187718293@ NOTE Gondioc
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Gondioc (also Gundioc, Gundowech, died 473) was king of Burgundy following the descruction of Worms by the Huns in 436, succeeding Gundahar. Gondioc married the sister of Ricimer, the Gothic general at the time ruling the Western 
1 CONC Roman Empire.
1 CONT
1 CONT Gundobad, the son of Gondioc, succeeded Ricimer in 472, but abdicated after the death of his father in the following year as Gondioc was succeeded by his brother Chilperic I. After the death of Chilperic, Burgundy was divided amon
1 CONC g the sons of Gondioc, Gundobad, Chilperic II, Godomar and Godegisel.
0 @N6000000002240782232@ NOTE He was related to the Visigothic kings and shared their Arian Christian
1 CONT faith. At his death, his kingdom was divided between his four sons, Gundobad,
1 CONT Godegesil, Chilperic, and Gundomar. Later, Gundobad murdered brother
1 CONT Chilperic and his consort/wife, forcing their two daughters to take refuge in
1 CONT Geneva with uncle Godegesil. Clovis, hearing good reports of the one
1 CONT daughter, Clotilda, obtained permission for marriage from Gundobad, a
1 CONT marriage yielding 4 sons, 3 to become future kings.
